<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nathuram Godse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nathuram Vinayak Godse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nathuram Godse was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nationalist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> who assassinated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>, shooting him in the chest three times at point blank range at a multi-faith prayer meeting in Birla House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-delhi">New Delhi</a>, on 30 January 1948. A member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-mahasabha">Hindu Mahasabha</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashtriya-swayamsevak-sangh">Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh</a> (RSS), he popularised the works of his mentor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vinayak-damodar-savarkar">Vinayak Damodar Savarkar</a>, who had formulated the ideology of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindutva">Hindutva</a>. He had plotted the killing with Narayan Apte and six others, and claimed that Gandhi had favoured the political demands of Indian Muslims during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/partition-of-india">partition of India</a>. He was sentenced to death and executed at the Ambala Central Jail on 15 November 1949.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nathuram-godse.jpg" alt="Nathuram Godse" width="312" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Indian Government work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nathuram_godse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Gandhi was shot dead in Delhi on 30 January 1948 by <b>Nathuram Godse</b>, a Hindu nationalist who blamed him for concessions to Muslims and Pakistan.</blockquote><a href="/movement/indian-independence-movement">Indian independence movement · Outcomes</a></li><li><blockquote>After <b>Nathuram Godse</b>, a former RSS volunteer, assassinated Mahatma Gandhi, Jawaharlal Nehru’s cabinet banned the RSS and arrested more than 200,000 volunteers; according to the political scientist Nandini Deo, the government’s commissions later found the RSS innocent of a role in the killing.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/hindutva">Hindutva · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>The Hindu nationalist <b>Nathuram Godse</b> shot Gandhi at a prayer meeting at Birla House.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-30">30 January in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Baramati, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in Ambala, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=18.15,74.58&amp;year=1935" aria-label="Baramati on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6572 1490 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Nathuram Godse"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7022 1760h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7022 1760h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=18.15,74.58&amp;year=1935">What was here in 1935? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
